FLAG — example.py, process_order function, credit limit check

The comparison operator is inverted. The code contains:
    if discounted_total <= remaining_credit:
        return {"approved": False, "reason": "credit_limit_exceeded", ...}

This rejects orders when the customer HAS sufficient credit (total is within limit). It should be:
    if discounted_total > remaining_credit:
        return {"approved": False, "reason": "credit_limit_exceeded", ...}

The operator `<=` expresses the opposite relation — it rejects when credit is adequate and would approve when credit is exceeded.
